// EXPECT: one error for the unclosed `{` of `main`, with the span pointing at
// the OPENING brace rather than at end of file
// RECOVER: exactly one error, and no cascade. Note that `after` will be parsed
// as a procedure NESTED inside `main`, not as a top-level one: nested
// procedures are legal in Jairs, so the parser genuinely cannot tell that a
// brace is missing until it reaches end of file. Pretending otherwise would
// require an indentation heuristic, which we deliberately do not use.
main :: () {
    a := 1;

after :: () {
}
